crates/bv/src/main.rs run_robot_search:
(1) Read --search-weights; if non-empty, parse it as a JSON object of f64 and port search.ParseWeightsJSON (pkg/search/config.go:115-152) in full, not just the required-key check:
   - JSON syntax error -> `Error: invalid weights JSON: {go_err}` (the inner text is Go's encoding/json wording, e.g. `invalid character 'o' in literal null (expecting 'u')`), exit 1;
   - for each of text, pagerank, status, impact, priority, recency in that fixed order, a missing key -> `Error: weights JSON missing {key:?}`, exit 1;
   - any key outside that set -> `Error: weights JSON has unknown key {key:?}`, exit 1;
   - then port Weights::validate (pkg/search/weights.go:27-75): every component must be finite -> `Error: weight {name:?} must be finite`; every component must be >= 0 -> `Error: weights must be non-negative`; the sum must be finite -> `Error: weights sum must be finite`; |sum-1.0| must be <= 0.001 -> `Error: weights must sum to 1.0, got {sum:.3}`. Any failure exits 1. This validation method does not exist in the Rust crate and must be written.
(2) Run this validation UNCONDITIONALLY (not only in the hybrid branch) so a bad value errors in text mode too — confirmed: `bv --search q --robot-search --search-weights notjson` exits 1 in Go.
(3) When validation passes, set a has_weights flag. In the HYBRID BRANCH ONLY this makes the resolved preset name "custom" (search_output.go:144-147) and causes weights to be emitted. In TEXT MODE emit neither preset nor weights — verified Go behaviour.
(4) Fall back to BV_SEARCH_WEIGHTS when the flag is absent (the only discard rule for weights is `if weightsFlag != "" { weights = "" }`).
(5) Feed the final weights into ranking_hash.

crates/bv/src/main.rs:177-200 — replace the presence.has("format")-gated block with Go's UNCONDITIONAL resolution (main.go:2029-2042 + 7567-7579), so it runs on every invocation before any dispatch:
  let cli = read_flag_eq_or_space(&args, "format");   // must handle "--format X" AND "--format=X" (and -f, already expanded by argv.rs)
  let resolved = cli.map(|s| s.trim().to_string()).filter(|s| !s.is_empty())
      .or_else(|| env_trimmed("BV_OUTPUT_FORMAT"))
      .or_else(|| env_trimmed("TOON_DEFAULT_FORMAT"))
      .unwrap_or_else(|| "json".to_string())
      .to_lowercase();
  if resolved != "json" && resolved != "toon" {
      eprintln!("Invalid --format {resolved:?} (expected json|toon)");
      return ExitCode::from(2);
  }
  if resolved == "toon" && !bv_robot::envelope::tru_available() {
      eprintln!("warning: tru not available; falling back to JSON");
      resolved = "json".into();
  }
  set_output_format(&resolved);
The trim is REQUIRED (Go trims; `--format " json "` must exit 0), and reading BOTH the space and equals forms is required (`--format=bogus` must exit 2, not silently become json).

